<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 10.17 pct.</title>
<headline>Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 10.17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia cut its internal coffee price by 10.17 percent Friday in the seventh such reduction since a new sliding-scale formula was introduced to adjust prices paid to growers on Jan. 31, the National Coffee Growers' Federation said.</p>
<p>It said the new price, effective until Friday of next week, had been set at 339.875 pesos per 125-kg load.</p>
<p>The cut was one of the sharpest since mid-June when the internal price was trimmed by 11.6 percent.</p>
<p>A federation spokesman said the new rate was based on the lowest trading price Colombian coffee had dropped to in New York over the past week -- $2.02 per pound.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
